==Intergovernmental relations with prefectural and metropolitan governments==

The Cabinet Office occupies the central coordinating junction linking national policy directives with the autonomous administrations of the forty-seven provincial prefectures and [[Okami Metropolis]]. Because the Cabinet Office formulates cross-cutting national policies that affect all subnational jurisdictions, its operational framework relies on formal consultative mechanisms rather than coercive mandates.

Intergovernmental coordination is conducted primarily through the Regional Revitalization Bureau and the Central Disaster Management Council. The Regional Revitalization Bureau administers the National Regional Revitalization Grant Facility, distributing capital funds directly to prefectural governments to finance local job creation, remote infrastructure, and public healthcare retention in depopulating regions such as [[Miyagi Prefecture]] and [[Noto Prefecture]]. The bureau maintains continuous liaison with the National Governors' Association, receiving input from prefectural governors on regional disparities and the fiscal burdens imposed by national mandates.

In disaster preparedness, the Cabinet Office operates the intergovernmental crisis communications network connecting the Prime Minister's Official Residence directly with all forty-eight prefectural emergency operation centers. Under the Disaster Countermeasures Basic Act, when a major disaster occurs, the Cabinet Office activates the Central Disaster Emergency Command, which coordinates the deployment of national relief funds, logistics, and Self-Defense Forces assets in direct collaboration with affected prefectural governors.

Relations with the [[Okami Metropolitan Government]] require specialized administrative mechanisms due to the capital's concentration of corporate power and autonomous municipal capabilities. The Cabinet Office and the Metropolitan Government maintain the Joint Capital Resilience Council, which coordinates urban crisis management, electrical grid decentralization, and flood defense along the Kumagawa River basin. While the Governor of Okami Metropolis commands substantial municipal tax wealth, the Cabinet Office retains statutory authority to set national urban development standards and disaster mitigation baselines that constrain metropolitan zoning and corporate data infrastructure.

==Key statutory legislation==

The Cabinet Office administers and executes core organic statutes governing executive operations and national planning:
the Cabinet Law of 1947, governing the collegial decision-making and resignation procedures of the executive;
the National Government Organization Act of 1948, establishing the statutory boundaries of line ministries and agencies;
the Cabinet Office Establishment Act of 1999, defining the coordinating jurisdiction, councils, and bureaus of the office;
the Basic Act for Gender Equal Society of 1999, establishing statutory frameworks for female representation and nondiscrimination;
the Disaster Countermeasures Basic Act of 1961, regulating intergovernmental emergency declarations and disaster relief;
and the National Police Act of 1954, defining the democratic supervisory authority of the National Public Safety Commission.

